WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.033
Answer relevancy.

2
00:00:02.333 --> 00:00:06.224
An answer can be perfectly grounded and still dodge the question.

3
00:00:06.224 --> 00:00:07.900
Faithfulness can't see that.

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:13.400
Answer relevancy asks: does the answer address the question that was asked?

5
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:20.000
An answer can summarize the wrong report, answer a related but different question, or hedge with filler.

6
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:24.533
Faithfulness can't see these failures, which is why the two metrics are a pair.

7
00:00:25.733 --> 00:00:27.433
RAGAS uses a clever trick.

8
00:00:27.733 --> 00:00:28.767
Take the answer.

9
00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:33.833
Ask an LLM to reverse engineer the questions this answer responds to.

10
00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.200
Embed those generated questions.

11
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.318
Then compare them by cosine similarity to the real question.

12
00:00:40.318 --> 00:00:43.055
On target means they land right next to it.

13
00:00:43.055 --> 00:00:44.900
A dodge lands somewhere else.

14
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.767
Picture it in embedding space.

15
00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:49.633
Here is the real question.

16
00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:54.367
If the answer is on target, the question guessed from it points almost the same way.

17
00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:59.000
If the answer dodged, the guessed question points elsewhere, and the score drops.

18
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.067
Here is the same trick by hand.

19
00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.600
Generate three questions from the answer.

20
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:09.133
Embed the real question and compare each guess with cosine similarity.

21
00:01:09.433 --> 00:01:11.633
The average is the answer relevancy.

22
00:01:12.833 --> 00:01:16.433
A user asks what caused the anomaly on sol one twenty two.

23
00:01:16.733 --> 00:01:22.300
Retrieval mostly surfaced sol one twenty one, so the model faithfully summarized that.

24
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:26.767
Faithfulness is point nine two, but relevancy is only point four one.

25
00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.963
The answer was well written, cited, and useless.

26
00:01:29.963 --> 00:01:35.333
Filter by sol number before the vector search, and relevancy climbs to point eight eight.

27
00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:37.296
Let's recap.

28
00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:40.600
Relevancy asks if the answer addresses the question.

29
00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.367
We reverse engineer questions and compare their embeddings.

30
00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:46.633
A faithful answer can still dodge.

31
00:01:46.933 --> 00:01:48.920
So use it with faithfulness.

32
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.333
Next up: the LLM as judge pattern.
